# No documentation updates

Skip docs by default so chats stay smaller. Do not create, edit, or append project documentation unless the user says in that message that documentation should be updated.

Leave these alone:

- `docs/DEVELOPMENTGUIDE.md`
- `docs/changes/**`
- `docs/DevelopmentHistory/**`
- `docs/adr/**`
- `README.md` and other `**/README.md`
- `App/Views/help/**`
- `docs/samples/**` guides (not Atom XML)
- `docs/.cursorrules`

Do not add “docs updated” notes, CHANGELOG entries, help copy, or development-history JSON as a side effect of a feature or content task.

# Keep Atom collections

Still create and save ready-to-import feeds under `docs/atoms-collections/` (new `.atom` files and edits to existing ones). That folder is content, not documentation.

```text
# ❌ BAD — content task also rewrites CHANGES / DEVELOPMENTGUIDE / Help / history JSON
# ✅ GOOD — write docs/atoms-collections/my-post.atom and stop
```

If `/paper-checkdocs` or the user says to update docs, follow that request for that turn only.
